 When the decision rests with a leader who has a documented pattern of announcing then reversing (Trump, 12.6), a credible strike-PLANNING report is NOT evidence of a strike - it is evidence of a NEGOTIATING POSTURE. The leak is often the instrument: the threat is made public precisely so it can be traded away. HARD RULE: absent a confirmed 'go' order or ordnance actually released, cap P(strike executes as reported) at 0.35, regardless of how strong the planning evidence looks (allied coordination, target lists, even market-hour sequencing). Escalate above 0.35 ONLY on capital-committed execution signals (aircraft launched, NOTAMs, carrier movement), never on reporting about intent.
 WHY THIS EXISTS: on 2026-07-31 CBS reported US+Israel planning their harshest-yet campaign on Iranian energy infrastructure, timed to conclude before markets opened Monday. The engine logged #72 at 0.55. It NAMED Trump's reversal pattern as 'the main brake' in that very prediction's sensitivity field - and still logged 0.55. Trump stood down the next night, citing 'perimeters of a deal'. This was the THIRD escalation-lean to fail (#63 Yemen strikes, #59 ceasefire-fails at risk, #72 energy strikes). Identifying a brake is not the same as WEIGHTING it - so the weighting is now a hard numeric cap, not a judgment call.
 COROLLARY: a stand-down is not a deal. Iran simultaneously denied movement toward a longer-term agreement. Do not flip from over-predicting escalation to over-predicting resolution - 16.12 oscillation cuts BOTH ways.
