+### 16.15 The Leg-Extrapolation Error - the engine's single largest loss source (2026-09-19 scoring cycle, 30 rows resolved against primary data)
+THE FINDING: across 44 scored rows, the calls that EXTRAPOLATED THE CURRENT LEG of the Iran/oil oscillation went 0-for-8 (mean Brier 0.47): #19 'no return to war-scale' and #28 'oil-down branch holds' (logged 7/8-9 while the ceasefire was collapsing), #29 'OPEC+ defends price into a glut' (7/11), then - after the war resumed - #59 'ceasefire fails', #63 'US strikes Yemen', #72 'energy-infrastructure strikes' (7/21-8/2, just as the pause arrived), then - after the pause - #74 'XLE beats USO as the premium unwinds' and #76 'pump prices fall below $4' (8/4, two sessions before Brent turned from 79 back to 94). Every OTHER row in the book went 33-for-36 (Brier 0.155). The engine was whipsawed THREE times in eight weeks, each time by the same move: treating the leg it was standing in as the regime. 16.12 already says the war oscillates; 16.14's corollary already says 'do not flip from over-predicting escalation to over-predicting resolution'. Naming it did not stop it - #74/#76 were logged the same day the MIRROR RISK warning was written into STATE.md. So it becomes a gate, not a warning.
+OBSERVED HALF-PERIOD: Apr-8 ceasefire -> Apr-22 blockade -> Jun-17 memorandum -> Jul-7 collapse -> ~Jul-30 pause -> Aug-31 round 3 -> ~Sep-10 fire pause. Legs last ~2-5 weeks. ANY iran-war / oil-direction call with a horizon beyond ~10 trading days therefore spans an expected reversal.
+THE LEG-NEUTRAL GATE (mandatory for cluster iran-war, oil-tape, opec-policy and any energy-direction row): (1) state the direction of the last 10 sessions of tape (Brent, transit counts, strike nights). (2) If the call's direction EQUALS it, the call is leg-extrapolation: cap P at 0.55, or re-express it as a physical invariant (below). (3) Write the reversal case into --sensitivity as a dated trigger, not a mood ('Brent back above 85 within 5 sessions kills this'). (4) Never log more than ONE new same-direction iran/oil row per session - the 7/8 batch (9 rows) and the 8/4 batch (6 rows) each shared one premise and lived or died together.
+WHERE THE EDGE ACTUALLY IS: in the same cluster, calls built on PHYSICAL or INSTITUTIONAL INVARIANTS went 8-for-8 (Brier 0.10): regime does not collapse (#17), Mojtaba stays invisible (#18), Hormuz does not normalize in 60d (#22) / by Friday (#73) - mine clearance and war-risk repricing are measured in weeks, more maritime attacks (#15), Saudi exports fall >20pct with both routes squeezed (#58), Brent prints 100 (#60), crude >85 passes through to a +0.4 CPI with a lag (#32). These do not care which leg is live. PREFER THEM: ask 'what is true in BOTH the escalation and the mediation world?' and stake that.
