+The 7/8 batch (#15,#17-#23) was logged 20:18-21:05Z on 7/8 on the premise 'the ceasefire holds'. Iran had struck three vessels in Hormuz on 7/7; the ceasefire was declared over on 7/8-9; transits went 49 -> 25/day by 7/9. #28 ('no Hormuz re-closure for 30 days') was logged 7/9 07:14Z with the re-closure already in the tape. The hits in that batch (#15, #20, #21) hit BECAUSE the premise was false (renewed war made attacks near-certain) - hits for the wrong reason. This is 16.13 (structural-state staleness) a second time, so it is mandatory: before ledgering ANY row whose premise is a STATE ('ceasefire holding', 'strait open', 'deal live', 'talks on', 'pause in effect'), find the most recent primary datapoint for that state variable - transit counts, strike logs, the mediator's last statement - dated within 24h of logging, and put its timestamp in the event field. No datapoint inside 24h -> the premise is UNVERIFIED -> cap conviction's precondition component at 0.00 and P at 0.55. `ledger.py add` now prints a STATE-PREMISE lint line when the wording trips it.
